VERDICT
  PROVED: noncommon walls split exactly into Farey/divisor owner sheets.
  PROVED: each owner set is a signed cyclic column word with the stated N_A(S).
  CORRECTED: K_7,7, K_7,8, and K_8,8 are known ordinary crossing cases.
  REFUTED: Zarankiewicz value, parity, cut, or crossing energy determines the sign.
  EVIDENCE: every bounded-bank owner word satisfies |t G_S|<1/2.
  NEXT: prove an adjacent-pin signed-word cap, starting with planar singleton sheets.
